<div class="institution-eligibility-outcome">
    <div class="institution-eligibility-outcome--{{type}}{{#hasPossibleMatches}} institution-eligibility-outcome--has-possible-matches{{/hasPossibleMatches}}">
        {{#isAgreed}}
            <h4 class="institution-eligibility-outcome__top_line">Your Institution has an on-going publishing agreement with eLife.</h4>

            <p class="institution-eligibility-outcome__text">
                Manuscripts are eligible for publication at no cost if <b>one of the corresponding authors is affiliated with the Institution/funder participating in the publishing agreement.</b>
            </p>
            <p class="institution-eligibility-outcome__text">
                Please select your Institution/funder during submission and we'll take care of the rest. If you’re ready,
                <a target="_blank" href="/about/submit-your-research"><b>start your submission</b></a> or learn more about <a target="_blank" href="/about/peer-review"><b>the eLife Model</b></a>.
            </p>
        {{/isAgreed}}
        {{#isAgreedHhmi}}
            <h4 class="institution-eligibility-outcome__top_line">Your institution has an on-going publishing agreement with eLife.</h4>

            <p class="institution-eligibility-outcome__text">
                Manuscripts are eligible to publish at no cost <b>if a laboratory head employed by HHMI or a member of such laboratory is first, last, or corresponding author/co-author.</b>
            </p>
            <p class="institution-eligibility-outcome__text">
                Please select your Institution/funder during submission and we'll take care of the rest.
                If you’re ready, <a target="_blank" href="/about/submit-your-research"><b>start your submission</b></a> or learn more about <a target="_blank" href="/about/peer-review"><b>the eLife Model</b></a>.
            </p>
        {{/isAgreedHhmi}}
        {{#isNotAgreedPublished}}
            <h4 class="institution-eligibility-outcome__top_line">
                Your Institution/funder does <u>not</u> have an on-going publishing agreement with eLife. However, authors affiliated with your Institution/funder have published in eLife during the last three years.
            </h4>
            <p class="institution-eligibility-outcome__text">
                Manuscripts published in eLife would be subject to our publishing fee of $3,750, which covers all
                elements of the publishing process (initial evaluation, staff checks, peer review, publication of the
                article, re-review, publication of subsequent versions, typesetting of the final version, and author proofing)
            </p>
            <p class="institution-eligibility-outcome__text">
                If you’re ready, <a target="_blank" href="/about/submit-your-research"><b>start your submission</b></a> or learn more about <a target="_blank" href="/about/peer-review"><b>the eLife Model</b></a>.
            </p>
            <p class="institution-eligibility-outcome__text">
                <b>Publishing fee waivers:</b> we will grant a full waiver for anyone who needs it – whether because of the local economy, career stage, termination of a grant, lack of funding, etc.
                Authors are expected to have explored all reasonable sources for paying the publication fee and may apply for a fee waiver during the submission process.
                See our <a href="https://elife-rp.msubmit.net/html/elife-rp_author_instructions.html#fees"><b>publishing fee waiver policy</b></a> for more information.
            </p>
        {{/isNotAgreedPublished}}
        {{#isNotAgreedNotPublished}}
            {{#hasPossibleMatches}}
                <div class="institution-eligibility-outcome__possible_matches-block">
                    <h4 class="institution-eligibility-outcome__possible_matches_top_line">Did you mean</h4>
                    <div class="institution-eligibility-outcome__possible_matches_link_block">
                        <ul>
                            {{#possibleMatches}}
                                <li>
                                    <a class="institution-eligibility-outcome__possible_matches_link" href="{{url}}">{{name}} ({{country}})</a>
                                </li>
                            {{/possibleMatches}}
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            {{/hasPossibleMatches}}
            {{^hasPossibleMatches}}
                <h4 class="institution-eligibility-outcome__top_line">
                    Your Institution/funder does not have an on-going publishing agreement with eLife.
                </h4>
            {{/hasPossibleMatches}}

            <p class="institution-eligibility-outcome__text">
                Manuscripts published in eLife would be subject to our publishing fee of $3,750, which covers all
                elements of the publishing process (initial evaluation, staff checks, peer review, publication of the
                article, re-review, publication of subsequent versions, typesetting of the final version, and author proofing)
            </p>

            <p class="institution-eligibility-outcome__text">
                If you’re ready, <a target="_blank" href="/about/submit-your-research"><b>start your submission</b></a> or learn more about <a target="_blank" href="/about/peer-review"><b>the eLife Model</b></a>.
            </p>

            <p class="institution-eligibility-outcome__text">
                <b>Publishing fee waivers:</b> we will grant a full waiver for anyone who needs it – whether because of the local economy, career stage, termination of a grant, lack of funding, etc.
                Authors are expected to have explored all reasonable sources for paying the publication fee and may apply for a fee waiver during the submission process.
                See our <a href="https://elife-rp.msubmit.net/html/elife-rp_author_instructions.html#fees"><b>publishing fee waiver policy</b></a> for more information.
            </p>
        {{/isNotAgreedNotPublished}}
    </div>
</div>
